# What "export-ignore" leaves out is what ships. It decides the composer dist
# Packagist builds *and* — since the publish workflow hands "git archive" output
# to "tailor create-artefact --path" instead of pointing it at the checkout —
# the zip attached to the GitHub release and uploaded to the TER. Tailor has its
# own hardcoded exclusion list and no notion of this file, so keeping the two
# artefacts in agreement means the export has to be the thing tailor packs.
#
# The list is therefore only about *tracked* entries. ".Build", ".cache", "var",
# ".agent", ".idea", ".envrc" and "composer.lock" are git-ignored and never
# reach an archive to begin with, which is why none of them appears below.

/.editorconfig export-ignore
/.gitattributes export-ignore
/.gitignore export-ignore
/.php-cs-fixer.cache export-ignore
/Build export-ignore
/Tests export-ignore
/.github export-ignore
/CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
/docs export-ignore
/AGENTS.md export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md export-ignore
/GEMINI.md export-ignore

